{"reason": "The baseline achieves Recall@10 of 0.58808 in only 4 minutes, leaving significant compute budget while suffering from critical information loss: the 3 GB link graph is collapsed into scalar degrees without tracking direct hyperlinks to candidate tracker domains, URL host matching is corrupted by character stripping, and 32 SVD dimensions heavily bottleneck lexical cues. Concurrently, the neural model predicts 355 trackers independently without modeling label co-occurrence ecosystems, and an aggressive negative focal penalty over-suppresses tail trackers on a limited 80k training sample.", "module": ["data_processing_and_feature_engineering", "model_design", "training_evaluation"], "plan": {"data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "WHAT: Extract direct tracker hyperlink signals from link-graph.parquet, correct URL classification hostname matching, expand TLD features to top 80, and scale TF-IDF TruncatedSVD from 32 to 128 components with entropy and vertical keyword indicators. WHY: Trackers are frequently hyperlinked directly in site source code, current .strip('www.') corrupts valid domain names (e.g., weather.com to eather.com), and 32 SVD components lose critical site category context. HOW: Stream link-graph.parquet to map out-edges against the 355 tracking_domain_ids into tracker-specific link flags, use regex re.sub(r'^www\d*\.', '', host) for exact URL matching, extract top 80 TLD indicators, compute character entropy and keyword indicators (shop, blog, news, forum, tv, gov), and fit TF-IDF (char_wb ngrams 3 to 5) with 128-dimensional TruncatedSVD. Interface constraints: Preserve output matrices X_train, X_val, X_test, Y_train, Y_val, target_domain_ids, and val_ground_truth.", "model_design": "WHAT: Enhance TrackerRankingResNet with a Label Co-occurrence Refinement Module and configure AsymmetricLoss with calibrated tail penalties. WHY: Web trackers operate in syndicate clusters (such as Google Analytics with Google Syndication or Yandex Metrica with LiveInternet), which standard independent linear output heads fail to capture. HOW: In TrackerRankingResNet, pass initial tracker logit projections through a residual label-interaction dense block with LayerNorm and GELU before final ranking, keeping empirical prior log-odds initialization on the projection head, and update AsymmetricLoss defaults to gamma_neg=2.5 and clip_margin=0.02 to mitigate tail tracker under-prediction. Interface constraints: Retain class signatures TrackerRankingResNet(in_features, num_trackers, ...) and AsymmetricLoss(gamma_neg, gamma_pos, clip_margin).", "training_evaluation": "WHAT: Scale the training domain pool from 80,000 to 160,000 domains and run a 12-epoch cosine annealing training loop with early stopping based on validation Recall@10. WHY: The baseline utilized only 4 minutes of the 30-minute limit, and doubling training instances substantially increases positive supervision for rare trackers without overfitting. HOW: Adjust the sampling pool logic to retain stratified tracker domain coverage while drawing 160,000 training domains and 10,000 validation domains, train with AdamW (lr=1e-3, weight_decay=1e-4) and CosineAnnealingLR across 12 epochs with batch size 512, saving the checkpoint with optimal validation Recall@10. Interface constraints: Maintain evaluate_model signature, log Final Validation Score, and produce submission files at submission/submission.tsv and submission/submission.csv with columns domain_id and tracking_domain_id."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
