{"reason": "The previous solution reached Recall@10 of 0.67547 in only 4 minutes, leaving significant compute headroom while suffering from objective misalignment (pure elementwise loss fails to optimize pairwise top-10 ranking), unguided label refinement (random linear projections miss empirical tracker syndicates), unidirectional link-graph features (omitting widget/badge in-links), and under-sampled rare trackers (160k domains). Applying bidirectional graph streaming and topical normalization in feature engineering, embedding training-derived co-occurrence diffusion with top-k pairwise ranking in model design, and scaling training to 220k domains with checkpoint averaging will directly optimize the Recall@10 metric within the 30-minute budget.", "module": ["data_processing_and_feature_engineering", "model_design", "training_evaluation"], "plan": {"data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "WHAT: Extract bidirectional tracker hyperlinks from link-graph.parquet (both host-to-tracker out-links and tracker-to-host in-links), expand domain lexical indicators to 24 commercial verticals, and convert URL classification counts into row-normalized probability distributions plus log-volume. WHY: Trackers like social widgets and auth badges frequently link back to host domains, and tracker adoption is heavily determined by domain vertical, which is better represented by scale-invariant normalized category proportions. HOW: In the link-graph streaming loop, record both out-edges from target domains to tracking domain IDs and in-edges from tracking domains to target domains, scan domain names across 24 vertical keywords (e.g., shop, blog, news, forum, tv, gov, ad, media, video, tech, health, game, finance, press), and normalize URL category frequencies per domain to sum to 1 while retaining log1p of total categorized URLs. Interface constraints: Preserve output matrices X_train, X_val, X_test, Y_train, Y_val, target_domain_ids, and val_ground_truth.", "model_design": "WHAT: Deepen TrackerRankingResNet to 384 hidden dimensions with 3 residual blocks, introduce an Empirical Tracker Co-occurrence Diffusion Layer, and integrate a smooth pairwise ranking loss with Asymmetric Loss (L_total = L_asym + 0.5 * L_rank). WHY: Web trackers exhibit deterministic co-occurrence clusters (such as Google Analytics with Google Ads and DoubleClick) that unconstrained linear layers fail to learn from scratch, and Recall@10 depends strictly on positive logits ranking above negative logits within the top 10 positions. HOW: Precompute the label conditional probability matrix P(tracker_j | tracker_i) from Y_train and propagate initial logits via a residual co-occurrence diffusion step with a learnable gate; formulate smooth pairwise ranking loss by computing log(1 + sum(exp(neg_logits - pos_logits))) across all valid positive-negative tracker pairs per sample. Interface constraints: Maintain TrackerRankingResNet class signature, ensure forward pass produces (batch_size, num_trackers) logits, and preserve loss module interface callable with logits and targets.", "training_evaluation": "WHAT: Expand the training domain sample pool from 160,000 to 220,000 domains, extend training to 14 epochs with Cosine Annealing, and implement Top-2 Checkpoint Weight Averaging before final test prediction. WHY: The previous run consumed only 4 minutes out of the 30-minute compute budget, and expanding domain coverage significantly enhances supervision on rare, long-tail trackers while checkpoint averaging smooths decision boundaries. HOW: Adjust the sampling logic to retain all 355 tracker stratified domains and sample up to 220,000 training domains and 10,000 validation domains; track the top 2 best validation Recall@10 checkpoints and average their model weights before generating final test rankings. Interface constraints: Maintain evaluate_model signature, log Final Validation Score, and output predictions to submission/submission.tsv and submission/submission.csv with columns domain_id and tracking_domain_id."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
