    "model_design": "WHAT: Deepen TrackerRankingResNet to 384 hidden dimensions with 3 residual blocks, introduce an Empirical Tracker Co-occurrence Diffusion Layer, and integrate a smooth pairwise ranking loss with Asymmetric Loss (L_total = L_asym + 0.5 * L_rank). WHY: Web trackers exhibit deterministic co-occurrence clusters (such as Google Analytics with Google Ads and DoubleClick) that unconstrained linear layers fail to learn from scratch, and Recall@10 depends strictly on positive logits ranking above negative logits within the top 10 positions. HOW: Precompute the label conditional probability matrix P(tracker_j | tracker_i) from Y_train and propagate initial logits via a residual co-occurrence diffusion step with a learnable gate; formulate smooth pairwise ranking loss by computing log(1 + sum(exp(neg_logits - pos_logits))) across all valid positive-negative tracker pairs per sample. Interface constraints: Maintain TrackerRankingResNet class signature, ensure forward pass produces (batch_size, num_trackers) logits, and preserve loss module interface callable with logits and targets.",
    "training_evaluation": "WHAT: Expand the training domain sample pool from 160,000 to 220,000 domains, extend training to 14 epochs with Cosine Annealing, and implement Top-2 Checkpoint Weight Averaging before final test prediction. WHY: The previous run consumed only 4 minutes out of the 30-minute compute budget, and expanding domain coverage significantly enhances supervision on rare, long-tail trackers while checkpoint averaging smooths decision boundaries. HOW: Adjust the sampling logic to retain all 355 tracker stratified domains and sample up to 220,000 training domains and 10,000 validation domains; track the top 2 best validation Recall@10 checkpoints and average their model weights before generating final test rankings. Interface constraints: Maintain evaluate_model signature, log Final Validation Score, and output predictions to submission/submission.tsv and submission/submission.csv with columns domain_id and tracking_domain_id."
