{"reason": "The baseline achieves Recall@10 of 0.8330 in only 5 minutes out of the 30-minute limit, leaving substantial compute headroom while suffering from three clear bottlenecks: 1) graph streaming collapses the 3 GB link graph into scalar degree counts instead of tracking direct out-links to specific tracker domains, while omitting explicit TLD identity and regional tracker priors; 2) the tracker interaction correlation matrix is initialized to zero rather than utilizing empirical label co-occurrence ecosystems, and lacks a direct residual path for direct tracker out-links; and 3) the margin ranking loss penalizes top-15 negatives rather than strictly aligning with the competition's top-10 evaluation boundary. Modifying feature engineering, model architecture, and training loss directly addresses these limitations to improve Recall@10.", "module": ["data_processing_and_feature_engineering", "model_design", "training_evaluation"], "plan": {"data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "WHAT: Record a 355-dimensional binary direct tracker link indicator vector during link-graph streaming, extract top 50 TLD one-hot features, and calculate out-of-fold TLD-conditional empirical tracker prior distributions. WHY: Sites frequently embed tracker widgets and tracking pixels as direct hyperlinks to tracker hostnames, providing deterministic identity signals that scalar degree counts discard, and web tracking practices are heavily regionalized by jurisdiction (e.g., Yandex on .ru, GDPR in EU). HOW: During link-graph streaming, check whether target_domain_id is in tracking_domain_to_id and populate a binary direct link matrix of shape (N, 355); parse domain hostnames to identify TLDs, one-hot encode the top 50 TLDs, compute smoothed empirical tracker frequencies per TLD on the training split, and concatenate these with base lexical and SVD features into X_train, X_val, and X_test with leak-free standard scaling. Interface constraints: Preserve arrays X_train, X_val, X_test, y_train_sparse, y_val_sparse, tracker_id_to_domain_arr, and test_domain_ids, ensuring direct-link indicators are appended at known feature indices.", "model_design": "WHAT: Initialize TrackerInteractionRankingNet's correlation matrix using normalized empirical tracker co-occurrence (PPMI), add a learnable residual projection from the 355-dimensional direct tracker link vector into logits, and update TopKMarginRankingLoss to top_k=10. WHY: Third-party trackers operate in syndicated bundles (e.g. Google Tag Manager with Analytics, LiveInternet with Yandex) which empirical co-occurrence captures from step 0, direct out-links should bypass deep representation bottlenecks, and ranking loss must align strictly with Recall@10. HOW: Compute train co-occurrence matrix C = Y_train.T @ Y_train, calculate positive pointwise mutual information (PPMI) with zeroed diagonals to initialize self.tracker_correlation, add self.direct_link_proj = nn.Linear(355, 355, bias=False) applied to the 355-dimensional tracker link input slice, and set top_k=10 in TopKMarginRankingLoss and HybridTrackerRankingLoss. Interface constraints: Retain class signatures TrackerInteractionRankingNet(in_features, num_trackers, ...) and HybridTrackerRankingLoss(gamma_neg, gamma_pos, margin, top_k, ranking_weight).", "training_evaluation": "WHAT: Extend training from 7 to 12 epochs using CosineAnnealingLR scheduling and maintain strict top-10 validation metric tracking with best checkpoint restoration. WHY: Baseline execution required only 5 minutes, leaving ample room within the 30-minute limit, and 12 epochs allows the residual direct link projection and correlation weights to converge thoroughly without overfitting. HOW: Configure CosineAnnealingLR(optimizer, T_max=12, eta_min=1e-5), train across 12 epochs with batch size 512, evaluate validation Recall@10 at each epoch with compute_validation_recall_at_10, save and reload the best model checkpoint from best_model_path, and export final predictions to submission/submission.tsv and submission/submission.csv. Interface constraints: Maintain compute_validation_recall_at_10 signature, log Final Validation Score, and produce submission files with domain_id and tracking_domain_id columns."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
