    "model_design": "WHAT: Initialize TrackerInteractionRankingNet's correlation matrix using normalized empirical tracker co-occurrence (PPMI), add a learnable residual projection from the 355-dimensional direct tracker link vector into logits, and update TopKMarginRankingLoss to top_k=10. WHY: Third-party trackers operate in syndicated bundles (e.g. Google Tag Manager with Analytics, LiveInternet with Yandex) which empirical co-occurrence captures from step 0, direct out-links should bypass deep representation bottlenecks, and ranking loss must align strictly with Recall@10. HOW: Compute train co-occurrence matrix C = Y_train.T @ Y_train, calculate positive pointwise mutual information (PPMI) with zeroed diagonals to initialize self.tracker_correlation, add self.direct_link_proj = nn.Linear(355, 355, bias=False) applied to the 355-dimensional tracker link input slice, and set top_k=10 in TopKMarginRankingLoss and HybridTrackerRankingLoss. Interface constraints: Retain class signatures TrackerInteractionRankingNet(in_features, num_trackers, ...) and HybridTrackerRankingLoss(gamma_neg, gamma_pos, margin, top_k, ranking_weight).",
    "training_evaluation": "WHAT: Extend training from 7 to 12 epochs using CosineAnnealingLR scheduling and maintain strict top-10 validation metric tracking with best checkpoint restoration. WHY: Baseline execution required only 5 minutes, leaving ample room within the 30-minute limit, and 12 epochs allows the residual direct link projection and correlation weights to converge thoroughly without overfitting. HOW: Configure CosineAnnealingLR(optimizer, T_max=12, eta_min=1e-5), train across 12 epochs with batch size 512, evaluate validation Recall@10 at each epoch with compute_validation_recall_at_10, save and reload the best model checkpoint from best_model_path, and export final predictions to submission/submission.tsv and submission/submission.csv. Interface constraints: Maintain compute_validation_recall_at_10 signature, log Final Validation Score, and produce submission files with domain_id and tracking_domain_id columns."
