    "model_design": "WHAT: Implement a Dual-Branch Tracker Network with direct residual skip paths for direct tracker in/out links, an NPMI-augmented dual tracker co-occurrence diffusion layer, and a Top-K Boundary Margin Ranking Loss. WHY: Direct hyperlinks between target domains and trackers represent deterministic 1-to-1 adoption signals that are diluted when compressed through a 384-dimensional dense bottleneck, empirical conditional co-occurrence heavily favors ubiquitous trackers over cohesive niche bundles, and global LogSumExp pairwise loss wastes gradients on hard positive outliers rather than candidates near the rank-10 boundary. HOW: In TrackerRankingResNet, route direct out-link and in-link feature slices through dedicated linear projections directly added to head logits; precompute a thresholded Normalized Pointwise Mutual Information (NPMI) matrix from Y_train and combine it with conditional co-occurrence via a learnable diffusion gate; and in TrackerRankingLoss, extract the top K=12 negative logits per sample to compute a softplus margin ranking loss against all positive logits alongside Asymmetric Focal Loss. Interface constraints: Preserve TrackerRankingResNet and TrackerRankingLoss class names, ensuring forward(x) outputs (batch_size, num_trackers) logits and loss(logits, targets) returns a scalar tensor."
