{"reason": "The baseline achieves 0.8450 Recall@10 in just 6 minutes but suffers from under-training (12 epochs while validation recall is monotonically climbing), information loss in compressed 32-dim SVD character representations, missed URL category mappings on subdomains, gradient vanishing from a 0.05 probability clipping dead-zone in AsymmetricFocalLoss, and under-utilized TLD priors collapsed through an MLP bottleneck. By refining feature extraction with 96 SVD components and root-domain URL fallbacks, incorporating a 2-hop residual graph diffusion layer with direct TLD log-prior logit injection, and extending training to 20 epochs with top-2 checkpoint averaging, we directly target the Recall@10 ranking objective within the 30-minute compute budget.", "module": ["data_processing_and_feature_engineering", "model_design", "training_evaluation"], "plan": {"data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "WHAT: Expand TruncatedSVD character n-gram dimensions from 32 to 96, implement root-domain fallback matching for URL category lookup, and calculate calibrated out-of-fold TLD log-odds tracker priors. WHY: 32 SVD components discard fine-grained domain subword variance across 400,000 domains, strict hostname matching fails for URLs with subdomains (e.g., blog.domain.com), and converting smoothed TLD probability estimates to log-odds log(p / (1 - p)) aligns with logit-space Bayesian modeling. HOW: Increase TruncatedSVD n_components to 96; in URL parsing, extract both full hostname and stripped registered domain (last two parts) to fall back when the exact hostname is missing; and convert out-of-fold TLD smoothed probabilities to log-odds clamped to [-6.0, 6.0], keeping known slice positions for model consumption. Interface constraints: Maintain X_train, X_val, X_test shapes, tracker indices, and downstream array dimensions.", "model_design": "WHAT: Upgrade the PPMI tracker interaction to a 2-hop residual gated graph diffusion block, introduce a dedicated TLD log-prior residual projection branch directly into the output layer, and remove negative probability clipping (clip=0.0) in AsymmetricFocalLoss. WHY: 1-step unparameterized correlation ignores multi-hop tracker syndicates, feeding TLD priors through the MLP forces hidden layers to re-learn geographical baseline distributions rather than domain-specific likelihood ratios, and clip=0.05 creates a gradient dead zone for negative candidates competing near the top-10 threshold. HOW: Implement a 2-hop graph diffusion layer where normalized PPMI message passing occurs twice with residual connections, layer norm, and learnable gating; slice the TLD log-prior features from the input tensor and project them directly into logit space via a learnable diagonal/linear layer added to base_logits; and instantiate AsymmetricFocalLoss with clip=0.0. Interface constraints: Preserve TrackerInteractionRankingNet forward pass returning (batch_size, num_trackers) logits and maintain HybridTrackerRankingLoss interface.", "training_evaluation": "WHAT: Expand training schedule from 12 to 20 epochs with a 2-epoch linear warmup followed by Cosine Annealing, and implement Top-2 checkpoint weight averaging for final inference. WHY: Validation Recall@10 was monotonically rising at epoch 12 (reaching 0.8450) and execution consumed only 6 minutes of the 30-minute limit, showing significant headroom for complete convergence, while checkpoint averaging smooths noisy decision boundaries near the top-10 rank boundary. HOW: Set num_epochs=20 with a linear warmup of 2 epochs before CosineAnnealingLR; at each epoch record validation Recall@10 and save the top 2 best checkpoint state dicts; average the weights of the top 2 checkpoints into the evaluation model before final validation and test set inference. Interface constraints: Preserve compute_validation_recall_at_10, log 'Final Validation Score', and maintain submission export format with columns domain_id and tracking_domain_id to ./submission/submission.csv and ./submission/submission.tsv."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
